    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini-ai\n\n### Description\n\nHey first and foremost thank you for this great plugin. \r\nI have noticed that after adding `mini.ai` change and deleting surrounding quotes with `nvim.surround` [smart aliasing](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround/blob/main/doc/nvim-surround.txt#L205) has stopped working and now it fails with \r\n```\r\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"a`\" found covering region within 50 lines and `search_method = 'cover_or_next'`.\r\n```\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Place the cursor inside the quote.\r\n2. Hit either `csq`/`dsq` to change/delete quotes.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should either change or delete surrounding quotes.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIt fails with the following error:\r\n```\r\n(mini.ai) No textobject \"a`\" found covering region within 50 lines and `search_method = 'cover_or_next'`.\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/45797239/202898288-a2ed675a-f68b-414f-b926-ac43912fe529.mov\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2022-11-20T12:06:39Z",
