        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> @echasnovski I need a bit more explanation because I think you misunderstood me a bit. From your video, I can see you have different behavior than I do. So the whole issue wasn't about the message but broken behavior. When you hit `csq\"` - it changes quotes for you, when I do - it doesn't - that's what I intended to report. Going to dig a bit more to find out what it is.\r\n\r\nIt probably is due to interference with some other plugin or Neovim setting. The usual approach to figuring it out is by disabling plugins in config until problem is gone. My initial guess would be that the problem is in either 'noice.nvim' or 'nvim-notify'.\r\n\r\nI used all default config for 'mini.ai' and 'nvim-surround':\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.ai').setup()\r\nrequire('nvim-surround').setup()\r\n```",
